# Trusted keys for this repository. One line per person or AI:
#
#   name@person  key-type  public-key
#   name@ai      key-type  public-key
#
# These are PUBLIC keys. They let anyone check a signature and let nobody make
# one, so this file is safe to publish. What must be protected is who can edit
# it: whoever can add a line here can grant access. Keep it on main.
#
# "argmap verify" reads this file from main and checks that every commit is
# signed by a key listed here, and that each review, piece of evidence and log
# entry a commit adds is in the signer's own name.
#
# To add yourself (once), with an SSH key you already use for GitHub:
#   git config gpg.format ssh
#   git config user.signingkey ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
#   git config commit.gpgsign true
# then add a line here with the contents of that .pub file after your name.
# Only ssh-ed25519 keys are checked for now.
#
# On a machine without ssh-keygen, "argmap use-key <private key file>" sets a
# clone up to sign with a small helper that ships with argmap.
#
# Text after a key is a free label saying which key it is. Two lines may carry
# the same name: one identity signing from two places.
#
aldrin@person ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIJOp/UAYTX6pE/zVydAdoiNfXCeFGgcmVWnykq7GTovu owner

